{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "93857ae6-9307-8e9d-9174-81d5839cfb6d",
  "created_at": "2026-03-12T10:33:29-04:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Angela Iannuccilli",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Priya Raman",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T10:31:15-04:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Utilities billing, this is Priya. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T10:31:19-04:00",
      "duration": 25,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yes, good morning. So I'm on speakerphone, I'm sorry, I'm carrying about four things right now. Um, my name is Angela Iannuccilli, and we closed on the house at 67 Memorial Boulevard, the Easton's Beach side, about three weeks ago, and I did all the change of address stuff, the electric, everything, and now the first water and sewer bill shows up and it's in the former owner's name. Not mine. His."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T10:31:44-04:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, that's common with a new sale. The account stays under the previous owner until we get the closing information. Do you have the bill in front of you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T10:31:54-04:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I do, yeah. And the other thing, the reading on it says estimated. Estimated! And I went and looked, the meter is down in the crawlspace, and nobody goes in there. I mean nobody. There's no way anybody read that. So I'm paying for a guess on somebody else's name, basically."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T10:32:11-04:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I understand. If the meter's in a crawlspace and no one has had access, an estimate is likely. We can set up an actual reading, and I'll note the account for the ownership change. Can you give me a callback number?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T10:32:25-04:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, it's 401-555-0190."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T10:32:27-04:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it, 401-555-0190. I'll flag it so someone contacts you to schedule the meter reading and update the name."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T10:32:34-04:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. And, so, I work days, like all day, I'm not out until after four. Can I pay this in person after four-thirty, or in the evening somewhere? Or is there some way that's not during your regular hours? I just want it handled."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T10:32:49-04:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The counter at City Hall closes with regular business hours, so after four-thirty in person won't work. There's a drop box for payments, and you can pay online anytime using the account number on the bill. Since the name is still the old owner's, the online account number should still work."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T10:33:06-04:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, online, fine. Good. My brother lives overseas, by the way, he's gonna hear about this call tonight, believe me. He thinks buying a house is the hard part."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T10:33:16-04:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "[pause] Well, hopefully the rest goes smoothly. I'll get this note in today, and someone will call you about the meter."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T10:33:24-04:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Great. Thanks, Priya."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-03-12T10:33:26-04:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome. Have a good day."
    }
  ],
